A||N||1||Capt Fiero||Piston blow-by||||1||
Z||000000||Capt Fiero||02-24-2000||07:33 PM||||AH, what is happening, Ok I am getting a bad case of blow by, I don't burn much oil maybe 1/2 qt in 3000 miles.  I don't blow blue out the tailpipe.  But I am getting oil into the intake tube and massive amounts of oil into the intake through the both the PCV pipe and the rear valve cover breather pipe.  Compression checks show 145-155 across the board. That is with all the plugs out and the throttle wide open during crank.  Is it head related or ring related.  What should I check. How do I check it.<P>Thanks For all your help, you all have been awsome.<P>David||||reg||1
Z||000001||1FST2M6||02-24-2000||07:44 PM||||odds are it's not piston blow by its a valve issue. replace the valve stem seals.. thats what i did and it fixed my problem... Also.. the tube that runs from the valve cover to the intake tube... if you drive you car rather hard a lot it will carry oil from the valve cover area in to the intake tube and cause it to look like blow by... you can plug the hole on the intake tube and place a tube with a K&N filer where the tube connects to the valve cover. placeing the filter in a catch can and this will catch all the oil that is being lost to high RPMs... obviously not to be used again but at least then you can see that your 1/2 in 3000 might not be burning...||||reg||1
